<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the WIDGET EXTENSION in the Developer ID (Homebrew) Mac
  Catalyst build. Separate from the app's Catalyst.entitlements because the
  two need different things, and the difference is not cosmetic.

  app-sandbox is mandatory HERE and absent there. macOS refuses to host an
  unsandboxed app extension at all: the bundle installs, pluginkit registers
  it, the widget shows up in the gallery, and then chronod fails every single
  timeline query with

    Failed to create extensionProcess … Code=16
      "Extension must have `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` entitlement."

  which leaves a widget that exists and never draws. Nothing before that point
  complains: the signature verifies, notarization is accepted, the App Group
  round-trips from the app side. Only chronod's log says why (2026-08-07).

  The host app is deliberately NOT sandboxed. It is a Developer ID app that
  reads and writes outside a container, and sandboxing it would need a much
  larger set of entitlements for no gain. An extension may be sandboxed while
  its host is not; the App Group is what bridges them.

  application-groups has to be repeated here. This is the READING side of the
  widget payload, and a sandboxed process reaches the Group Container only if
  it claims the group itself. Entitle just the app and the widget renders an
  empty card.

  And the identifier is the team-ID-prefixed one, not the plain iOS
  `group.com.prayerapp`: with the plain name this extension faulted on every
  read under chronod. MihrabAppGroup.m has the evidence and its limits.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>GAW23HT439.group.com.prayerapp</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
